Hi,

so R has definitely a problem inferring the correct file access rules
for you, e.g. file.info <http://file.info>() reports octmode '511' which means read and
executable access but not write for that directory.  This is also
confirmed by the file.access() function of R.  Recognizing these kind
of problems, the fileAccess() of R.utils was designed to try to do
more robust tests.  However, I never created such a special test for
write permission of *directories*, but now I have.  Before making it
into the R.utils package, could you try to see what the following
outputs:

library("R.utils");
# Make sure the following line doesn't give an error
source("http://www.braju.com/R/patches/R.utils/20100905/fileAccess.R");
str(fileAccess.default);

path <- "Y:/cchen/AS&Methy/probeData/tissues,RBC/HuGene-1_0-st-v1";
print(fileAccess(path, mode=0));

print(fileAccess(path, mode=1));

print(fileAccess(path, mode=2));

print(fileAccess(path, mode=4));

If fileAccess(path, mode=2) returns 0 (instead of -1) as before, then
we have something that works.

/Henrik

