Hi Leif.

I actually never had verified that one can do PCR fragment-length
normalization on the MOUSEDIVm520650 chip type.  It turns out that the
current method/estimator/algorithm [1] does not support this chip
type.

The reason is as follows.  The Affymetrix assay for this chip type
digests/fragments the DNA using two restriction enzymes.  This is also
the case for chip types such as GenomeWideSNP_6. This means that any
unit (SNP or non-polymorphic locus) of interest will originate from a
DNA fragment that was digested by either one of the two enzymes or
both enzymes.  For GenomeWideSNP_6 it is the case that there exists
lots of units that are originating only from one of the enzymes.
These are the ones we use to estimate the PCR fragment-length effects,
but do not use the ones that are on both, cf. [1].  Unfortunately, it
is the case that for MOUSEDIVm520650 all units are sitting of
fragments originating from both enzymes, which means there are no
"single-enzyme" data points.  Hence the error message (FYI, in the
next release of aroma.light the error message will be more
informative).  Here is how you can see that all units are from both
enzymes:

> library("aroma.affymetrix");
> ufl <- AromaUflFile$byChipType("MOUSEDIVm520650");
> print(ufl);

